+### Compound Durations
+
+Use `parseCompound` to sum several parts into one value. Parts can be separated by whitespace, a comma, or nothing at all, and every part must have a unit.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours'); // 187200000
+parseCompound('1h30m15s'); // 5415000
+```
+
+Unlike `parse`, it throws a `TypeError` for invalid input (for example `"1h 30"`, which has no unit on the second part) rather than returning `NaN`.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
